  "derivation_note": "hold_duty is derived from the measured full-power and passive-cooling rates, not measured directly: dT/dt = c(T) + u*(h(T)-c(T)) = 0 gives u = -c/(h-c). Valid only over 60-190 C, the range the step test covered with enough samples. The 200 C point was dropped as an artefact -- the run stopped at 200.4 C, so both curves are sparse and the cooling data there is contaminated by the coast. Reflow peaks at 225-235 C sit ABOVE this range and are extrapolation until a higher step test extends it.",
